0..74 Comment "// The hole rust-lang/rust 164250 names: a struct\'s bound `T : \'static` is"
75..154 Comment "// checked when `Q(None)` is built and assumed by its destructor; the covariant"
155..235 Comment "// assignment `q.0 = Some(&l)` then re-instantiates `Q` at the local\'s lifetime,"
236..315 Comment "// and the destructor stores a view of `l` where only a `\'static` value may go."
316..396 Comment "// Here the region a slot keeps is part of the slot\'s type, a built value\'s type"
397..478 Comment "// never changes under it, and a destructor is a region\'s end action that reaches"
479..552 Comment "// only what the region keeps: the write is refused before anything runs."
553..555 Comment "//"
556..633 Comment "// What the hole is made of: evidence in two currencies. A bound written on a"
634..712 Comment "// type\'s definition is a side condition outside the value, re-proved at every"
713..791 Comment "// explicit use (a call, a coercion) but inherited as an assumption by the one"
792..871 Comment "// consumer with no use site, the destructor — an explicit `Drop` must repeat"
872..953 Comment "// the type\'s bounds exactly and so assumes them, and the generated drop glue has"
954..1033 Comment "// none — while subtyping by variance changes the type beneath it and nothing"
1034..1114 Comment "// re-establishes the bound. The same shape is the ergonomic rule \"bounds on the"
1115..1193 Comment "// impl, never on the struct\": a bound on the definition is re-stated on every"
1194..1273 Comment "// implementation and constrains every use. Here a constraint is a field of the"
1274..1351 Comment "// value\'s record, carried and projected, never implied from a definition and"
1352..1427 Comment "// never assumed by an implementation; the region is that field for a slot."
1428..1430 Comment "//"
1431..1446 Comment "// - see: #1492"
1448..1479 Comment "// Early exit\'s host interface."
